  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Colpitts oscillator"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "In a Colpitts oscillator the capacitor is split into $C_1$ and $C_2$ in series, with their junction at AC ground, and a single coil L across them. The feedback is taken from the capacitive divider. The tank capacitance is the series value $C_T = C_1C_2/(C_1 + C_2)$ and $f = 1/(2\\pi\\sqrt{L C_T})$. Because the transistor capacitances appear across $C_1$ and $C_2$ and can be absorbed into them, the Colpitts oscillator gives better frequency stability and is preferred at high frequencies."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Split capacitor C1, C2; one coil"
    },
    {
     "en": "CT = C1C2/(C1 + C2)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Better stability at high frequencies"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The Colpitts oscillator splits the capacitor. Use the series combination of C1 and C2 in the frequency formula.",
    "kn": "ಕಾಲ್ಪಿಟ್ಸ್ ಆಂದೋಲಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಧಾರಕ C1, C2 ಆಗಿ ವಿಭಜಿತ. ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗೆ ಅವುಗಳ ಸರಣಿ ಮೌಲ್ಯ CT = C1C2/(C1 + C2) ಬಳಸುತ್ತೇವೆ."
   },
   "formula": "f = \\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{L\\,C_T}}, \\qquad C_T = \\frac{C_1 C_2}{C_1 + C_2}"
  },
